technology.technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesse:
The pulp, or fibres from the wood are separated in a kraft cooking process in a so-called fibre line. In a recovery line, the chemicals used in the cooking process are recovered to be used again and energy is produced. The third process is effluent treatment where gaseous and liquid discharges to the environment are continuously minimized and monitored. The process includes transports to the pulp mill, wood handling, chemical pulping and bleaching, drying process, energy production on-site, recovery cycles of chemicals and internal waste water treatment. The input of magnesium sulphate (0.00104 kg/kg) has been excluded from the inventory since its contribution was less than 3 % in terms of mass and single score. The following air emissions were reported in the study: CO2 (fossil and biogenic), CO, SOx (as SO2), NOx, TRS (as S), SO2 (reported as S), Dust (unspecified). Next to these key emissions, additional emissions from on-site energy production from external and internal fuels were calculated, using emission profiles from ecoinvent combustion processes. Internal biogenic fuels are represented by the calculated emissions but do not have the corresponding fuel input from technosphere, because they are supplied from within the system boundaries. The amounts of internal fuels used in the process are: Bark (8.85E+02 MJ/t), -Black liquor (1.33E+04 MJ/t), Sludge (2.70E+01 MJ/t), and Methanol (2.25E+02 MJ/t).
The following ecoinvent combustion processes were used to estimate additional air emissions: Biofuel - Bark: heat production, wood chips from industry, at furnace 1000kW, CH; Methanol: heat production, natural gas, at industrial furnace >100kW, Europe without Switzerland; Natural gas: heat production, natural gas, at industrial furnace >100kW, Europe without Switzerland; Heavy fuel oil: heat production, heavy fuel oil, at industrial furnace 1MW, Europe without Switzerland; Light fuel oil: heat production, light fuel oil, at industrial furnace 1MW, Europe without Switzerland; Coke: heat production, at coal coke industrial furnace 1-10MW; propane: heat production, propane, at industrial furnace >100kW;
Black liquor and sludge were not included in the emissions calculations because no specific emission profiles, e.g. for the black liquor recovery process, were available. Emissions from these internal energy generation processes are therefore only reflected in the key emission factors provided by the industry, other emissions constitute a data gap. The amount of infrastructure (pulp factory) was taken from the dataset "The European Pulp Industry Sector Association AISBL, sulfate pulp production, from eucalyptus, bleached, RLA, Undefined, ecoinvent database version 3.7.1."
